1
00:01:51,421 --> 00:01:53,001
In 1014,

2
00:01:53,631 --> 00:01:54,631
York

3
00:01:54,711 --> 00:01:59,091
was controlled by the Vikings of Denmark,
led by King Sweyn.

4
00:01:59,931 --> 00:02:02,301
The land was used as a base

5
00:02:02,391 --> 00:02:05,931
for exporting slaves all over Europe.

6
00:02:06,021 --> 00:02:07,271
The Vikings served as

7
00:02:07,481 --> 00:02:11,061
slave traders.

8
00:02:13,321 --> 00:02:15,571
I know how you feel, boss.

9
00:02:16,441 --> 00:02:19,071
But we're not rich enough to free the slaves

10
00:02:19,151 --> 00:02:19,991
Reunion

11
00:02:20,071 --> 00:02:21,161
out of compassion.

12
00:02:22,491 --> 00:02:24,741
It's been 11 years already.

13
00:02:25,451 --> 00:02:28,211
Isn't it about time now?

14
00:02:30,371 --> 00:02:33,541
That day, without Thors,

15
00:02:33,631 --> 00:02:36,171
we wouldn't have gotten out of there alive.

16
00:02:37,881 --> 00:02:40,341
I must repay him for his help.

17
00:02:43,551 --> 00:02:45,471
Hurry! All of these over here!

18
00:02:45,561 --> 00:02:48,181
-Over there!
-Hurry! Go!

19
00:02:48,271 --> 00:02:49,231
What?

20
00:02:49,811 --> 00:02:50,981
Hey! You!

21
00:02:51,811 --> 00:02:54,691
You in the dirty cargo ship!
Get that ship out of the way!

22
00:02:56,111 --> 00:02:59,611
Hurry up! The first ship's almost here--

23
00:03:00,361 --> 00:03:01,781
Heave ho!

24
00:03:01,861 --> 00:03:04,951
Heave ho! Heave ho!

25
00:03:05,281 --> 00:03:08,831
Hurry up! A nobleman's ships

26
00:03:08,911 --> 00:03:10,711
are about to pull in along this pier!

27
00:03:10,831 --> 00:03:12,001
I got it.

28
00:03:16,591 --> 00:03:18,011
So, this is York.

29
00:03:19,421 --> 00:03:20,721
It's a big town.

30
00:03:21,301 --> 00:03:25,761
Yes. It's an old town that prospered
in the days of the Roman Empire.

31
00:03:26,681 --> 00:03:31,271
People and goods from both Northern Europe
and England all gather here.

32
00:03:32,441 --> 00:03:37,191
His Highness the king must be planning to
establish the capital of his new dynasty here.

33
00:03:37,901 --> 00:03:41,361
It's a good decision. I'd do the same thing.

34
00:03:44,411 --> 00:03:47,201
Come on! Who cares if they're nobility?

35
00:03:47,951 --> 00:03:49,791
Those guys are a pain. Damn.

36
00:03:50,961 --> 00:03:53,291
Hey, boss. Take care of the one on the stern.

37
00:03:58,501 --> 00:03:59,631
That man...

38
00:04:01,011 --> 00:04:03,341
That's right. It's definitely him.

39
00:04:04,131 --> 00:04:06,971
I'd never forget that face.

40
00:04:08,721 --> 00:04:13,441
Askeladd! The pirate who killed Thors!

41
00:04:14,141 --> 00:04:16,941
-Hey! Don't push!
-Who's ships are those?

42
00:04:17,021 --> 00:04:18,731
-Prince Canute's.
-What will you do?

43
00:04:19,571 --> 00:04:22,151
The king is going to strike at tomorrow's banquet.

44
00:04:22,361 --> 00:04:25,321
Well, about that...

45
00:04:26,451 --> 00:04:31,201
It's obvious that we're going to lose out
at the Imperial Council tomorrow.

46
00:04:32,001 --> 00:04:34,331
For example, he could give different territories

47
00:04:34,421 --> 00:04:37,211
to you and Thorkell to isolate you.

48
00:04:37,291 --> 00:04:40,251
He'd be giving you a reward,
but he'd also be giving you an order.

49
00:04:41,631 --> 00:04:45,261
If you refused, you'd be suspected
of harboring rebellious intentions.

50
00:04:45,721 --> 00:04:48,471
It's all up to the king what he wants to do with you.

51
00:04:49,261 --> 00:04:51,641
If he takes Thorkell from us, we're in trouble.

52
00:04:52,221 --> 00:04:54,271
True. We'd be in trouble.

53
00:04:55,601 --> 00:04:58,111
So... What's the plan?

54
00:05:01,731 --> 00:05:02,991
How about this?

55
00:05:03,401 --> 00:05:07,661
We could try exposing the secret
to the people around here.

56
00:05:07,781 --> 00:05:08,911
Exposing the secret?

57
00:05:09,071 --> 00:05:10,331
Which one is the prince?

58
00:05:10,411 --> 00:05:12,081
Isn't that him?

59
00:05:12,161 --> 00:05:13,701
Your Highness Canute.

60
00:05:16,001 --> 00:05:17,961
I mean that you're going

61
00:05:19,081 --> 00:05:21,301
to die here right now.

62
00:05:32,511 --> 00:05:34,481
He got shot!

63
00:05:35,311 --> 00:05:37,941
His Highness the Prince got shot!

64
00:05:38,151 --> 00:05:40,191
-Raise your shields!
-Where'd it come from?

65
00:05:40,271 --> 00:05:42,611
From the north bank! Find them!

66
00:05:43,821 --> 00:05:46,241
He was shot from this side? Unbelievable.

67
00:05:47,201 --> 00:05:48,741
What an easy job.

68
00:05:55,791 --> 00:05:57,081
Hey!

69
00:05:57,161 --> 00:05:58,501
What's happening?

70
00:05:58,921 --> 00:06:01,001
This is bad.

71
00:06:01,091 --> 00:06:03,381
We better not get involved in this.

72
00:06:03,551 --> 00:06:05,421
Hey! Where are you going, boss?

73
00:06:06,261 --> 00:06:08,131
It's him! He was there!

74
00:06:12,511 --> 00:06:13,601
What's wrong?

75
00:06:15,181 --> 00:06:16,811
Are you okay?

76
00:06:16,981 --> 00:06:18,561
You're bleeding!

77
00:06:32,871 --> 00:06:35,161
You wasted so much of my time.

78
00:06:54,561 --> 00:06:57,101
Hey! You bastards!

79
00:06:57,851 --> 00:06:59,561
What's going on?

80
00:06:59,641 --> 00:07:02,561
I bet you're the snipers!

81
00:07:03,481 --> 00:07:06,651
He's the sniper. It wasn't me. Here's the weapon.

82
00:07:07,861 --> 00:07:09,361
What's that?

83
00:07:09,531 --> 00:07:12,201
-Is it a bow?
-That's the weapon?

84
00:07:12,281 --> 00:07:14,371
Is he your friend?

85
00:07:14,451 --> 00:07:15,451
No, I--

86
00:07:15,531 --> 00:07:17,951
You can't fool us!

87
00:07:18,041 --> 00:07:20,501
You're just trying to blame everything on him

88
00:07:20,581 --> 00:07:22,421
and save yourself!

89
00:07:22,501 --> 00:07:23,961
I said it wasn't me!

90
00:07:24,131 --> 00:07:26,461
No! I can tell from your eyes!

91
00:07:26,551 --> 00:07:29,171
Your eyes are so murky.

92
00:07:29,261 --> 00:07:32,131
It's so obvious that you're a villain--

93
00:07:37,561 --> 00:07:39,221
Don't resist, you bastard!

94
00:07:39,311 --> 00:07:41,021
Wait! Wait! Wait!

95
00:07:41,981 --> 00:07:43,231
He's using a knife.

96
00:07:43,941 --> 00:07:45,771
He's small and he's young.

97
00:07:46,611 --> 00:07:48,691
Are you...

98
00:07:49,821 --> 00:07:51,571
Thorfinn Karlsefni?

99
00:07:51,651 --> 00:07:52,651
Thorfinn?

100
00:07:53,531 --> 00:07:54,621
Karlsefni?

101
00:07:55,491 --> 00:07:56,581
Who is he?

102
00:07:56,661 --> 00:07:58,411
You idiot! Don't you know who he is?

103
00:07:58,491 --> 00:08:02,331
He's the man who won a duel against
Thorkell the Tall with only two knives!

104
00:08:02,411 --> 00:08:04,001
What? No way!

105
00:08:04,881 --> 00:08:06,131
In that case, this is bad.

106
00:08:06,291 --> 00:08:08,381
He's one of His Highness's vassals.

107
00:08:08,461 --> 00:08:09,301
Seriously?

108
00:08:09,381 --> 00:08:11,261
Excuse me for a bit.

109
00:08:12,931 --> 00:08:13,881
You...

110
00:08:14,431 --> 00:08:15,641
Are you...?

111
00:08:16,641 --> 00:08:19,061
You're from Iceland, right?

112
00:08:21,771 --> 00:08:22,601
Your name

113
00:08:23,521 --> 00:08:26,191
is Thorfinn, son of Thors!

114
00:08:29,361 --> 00:08:30,231
You're...

115
00:08:31,071 --> 00:08:32,781
Leif.

116
00:08:38,951 --> 00:08:41,951
You're alive! I'm so glad.

117
00:08:42,411 --> 00:08:44,871
I'm so glad!

118
00:08:46,421 --> 00:08:47,711
Out of the way!

119
00:08:47,881 --> 00:08:49,211
Don't shake him, you idiot!

120
00:08:49,381 --> 00:08:50,211
Where was he hit?

121
00:08:50,301 --> 00:08:51,211
His chest. It's bad!

122
00:08:51,381 --> 00:08:52,971
Your Highness! Hold on!

123
00:08:53,131 --> 00:08:55,591
Your Highness! We're going to cut off your clothes.

124
00:09:09,731 --> 00:09:13,571
I had that feeling all along.

125
00:09:15,491 --> 00:09:17,991
His Highness is a woman!

126
00:09:18,071 --> 00:09:20,831
-This is big news!
-No way!

127
00:09:20,911 --> 00:09:22,081
You idiots.

128
00:09:24,121 --> 00:09:25,581
I'm right here.

129
00:09:27,871 --> 00:09:28,961
You're right.

130
00:09:32,551 --> 00:09:34,211
Why did you choose a woman?

131
00:09:34,461 --> 00:09:38,681
We couldn't find any male slaves who looked similar.

132
00:09:40,801 --> 00:09:41,721
Can you save her?

133
00:09:43,101 --> 00:09:45,931
No. Not with where she got shot.

134
00:09:46,021 --> 00:09:50,061
If there was poison on the arrow,
then she's probably already...

135
00:09:53,401 --> 00:09:54,821
I'm sorry.

136
00:09:59,491 --> 00:10:01,411
Take care of her.

137
00:10:01,871 --> 00:10:03,951
Do everything you can.

138
00:10:04,451 --> 00:10:05,291
Yes.

139
00:10:08,251 --> 00:10:10,041
Well, you know...

140
00:10:10,131 --> 00:10:13,301
Your precautions have paid off, Your Highness.

141
00:10:14,171 --> 00:10:18,341
It seems that there are people hiding here in York

142
00:10:18,431 --> 00:10:20,391
who want to do you harm.

143
00:10:24,141 --> 00:10:25,181
I see.

144
00:10:26,271 --> 00:10:27,981
You want to get revenge.

145
00:10:28,691 --> 00:10:32,271
Yes. I'm going to kill him, no matter what.

146
00:10:32,861 --> 00:10:35,821
With my father's dagger.

147
00:10:37,691 --> 00:10:39,911
He's all beaten up.

148
00:10:40,911 --> 00:10:44,161
A young child survived on the battlefield.

149
00:10:44,701 --> 00:10:47,121
I'm sure he's seen hell.

150
00:10:48,711 --> 00:10:50,421
No. I can't.

151
00:10:50,501 --> 00:10:52,171
In order to save this child,

152
00:10:52,251 --> 00:10:55,461
I have to forget these last 11 years.

153
00:10:56,591 --> 00:10:57,591
Leif.

154
00:10:59,011 --> 00:11:01,891
What's happening in Vinland right now?

155
00:11:03,551 --> 00:11:05,471
My father had wanted to go there.

156
00:11:06,391 --> 00:11:08,271
I dream about it sometimes too.

157
00:11:09,141 --> 00:11:11,061
Did you build a village already?

158
00:11:13,151 --> 00:11:16,861
Why aren't you asking me about your mother
and your sister, who you left behind?

159
00:11:17,861 --> 00:11:21,991
After you left, Helga's health got worse.

160
00:11:23,161 --> 00:11:25,281
Go see her, Thorfinn.

161
00:11:25,911 --> 00:11:27,831
It would make Helga feel better--

162
00:11:27,911 --> 00:11:30,581
I'm asking you about Vinland!

163
00:11:31,501 --> 00:11:34,081
Don't talk to me about things I didn't ask you!

164
00:11:34,711 --> 00:11:38,421
Hey. Hey! Where are you going? Thorfinn!

165
00:11:40,921 --> 00:11:43,051
Let's go home, Thorfinn.

166
00:11:43,141 --> 00:11:46,351
You've had enough, right? Let's go home together.

167
00:11:48,181 --> 00:11:49,221
Enough?

168
00:11:51,521 --> 00:11:53,311
You have no idea.

169
00:11:54,731 --> 00:11:56,521
You don't know anything about

170
00:11:56,611 --> 00:11:58,611
what I went through between that day and today.

171
00:11:59,191 --> 00:12:00,031
Right?

172
00:12:01,361 --> 00:12:02,901
As long as Askeladd

173
00:12:02,991 --> 00:12:06,741
is still alive, eating and shitting, it'll never be enough!

174
00:12:07,411 --> 00:12:09,241
It'll never be enough!

175
00:12:13,421 --> 00:12:15,631
How could this have happened?

176
00:12:16,591 --> 00:12:19,091
That cheerful young child.

177
00:12:26,801 --> 00:12:30,271
I'm going to stay in this town
until you change your mind!

178
00:12:31,731 --> 00:12:32,641
Thorfinn!

179
00:12:33,441 --> 00:12:35,191
Let's go home!

180
00:12:38,901 --> 00:12:40,531
Hey. Here's some booze.

181
00:12:42,611 --> 00:12:43,781
Thanks.

182
00:12:43,861 --> 00:12:46,991
Nice room, Bjorn. I'm jealous.

183
00:12:49,371 --> 00:12:52,541
This room is too small of a reward
for risking my life.

184
00:12:54,961 --> 00:13:00,801
By the way,
Atli said he wanted to apologize to you.

185
00:13:02,421 --> 00:13:06,301
I've got no hard feelings for anyone
who cut me on the battlefield.

186
00:13:07,801 --> 00:13:11,061
Thorfinn's the only one who holds a grudge about it.

187
00:13:13,891 --> 00:13:15,351
I'm okay. So go.

188
00:13:15,441 --> 00:13:17,271
It's time for you to make your evil plans.

189
00:13:18,731 --> 00:13:20,771
Yeah. See you later.

190
00:13:24,191 --> 00:13:25,201
Askeladd.

191
00:13:29,621 --> 00:13:32,411
How is your leg?

192
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:39,331
Well, I've been hit by a lot of arrows.

193
00:13:39,921 --> 00:13:41,131
But, well...

194
00:13:42,301 --> 00:13:45,171
It's good enough for me to hold a sword.

195
00:13:46,971 --> 00:13:47,881
I see.

196
00:13:49,391 --> 00:13:50,601
Then tomorrow.

197
00:13:52,811 --> 00:13:53,851
Okay.

198
00:13:55,021 --> 00:13:55,851
Tomorrow.

199
00:14:01,821 --> 00:14:04,901
We've been outwitted, Floki.

200
00:14:06,241 --> 00:14:07,991
I apologize.

201
00:14:11,321 --> 00:14:14,331
Askeladd? He's doing well.

202
00:14:16,451 --> 00:14:20,001
He's laid a curse on this town.

203
00:14:24,591 --> 00:14:26,551
The prince got killed?

204
00:14:26,631 --> 00:14:28,841
No! It was a double.

205
00:14:30,761 --> 00:14:32,051
It's so dangerous out there.

206
00:14:32,141 --> 00:14:35,271
We can't sleep in peace at night.

207
00:14:39,271 --> 00:14:41,651
What I don't understand

208
00:14:41,731 --> 00:14:45,821
is why the assassin was targeting the prince?

209
00:14:45,901 --> 00:14:48,401
Well, he's an important person!

210
00:14:48,491 --> 00:14:50,321
Of course someone would want to kill him!

211
00:14:50,491 --> 00:14:54,621
But King Sweyn is here!

212
00:14:54,701 --> 00:14:57,251
If they were going to go after someone, it would be him!

213
00:14:57,331 --> 00:14:58,871
Oh, you're right.

214
00:14:58,961 --> 00:15:01,831
And there are two heirs.

215
00:15:01,921 --> 00:15:05,631
So the fact that they went after the younger brother
must mean that...

216
00:15:05,711 --> 00:15:06,761
You there!

217
00:15:07,711 --> 00:15:11,301
I have some interesting information regarding that.

218
00:15:13,641 --> 00:15:14,971
Well,

219
00:15:15,061 --> 00:15:17,771
it's only a rumor, after all.

220
00:15:19,101 --> 00:15:21,481
Only a rumor?

221
00:15:21,561 --> 00:15:23,231
That's perfect.

222
00:15:24,811 --> 00:15:26,731
It's better not to offer definite proof.

223
00:15:26,821 --> 00:15:29,941
We should leave the king with some room.

224
00:15:31,571 --> 00:15:34,371
So you're the one who hired the assassin?

225
00:15:34,451 --> 00:15:36,121
You performed a part in your own play?

226
00:15:36,831 --> 00:15:39,121
It was some good acting, right?

227
00:15:39,201 --> 00:15:42,081
Spreading rumors isn't enough.

228
00:15:42,711 --> 00:15:47,381
That acting made the rumor seem real.
That's how the rumor will spread.

229
00:15:48,671 --> 00:15:51,881
Everyone knows of the dispute over succession
within Denmark's royal family.

230
00:15:52,051 --> 00:15:55,181
Now, there's been an assassination attempt,
and the rumors will spread.

231
00:15:55,801 --> 00:15:57,011
Well then, everyone.

232
00:15:57,601 --> 00:16:01,101
How is this going to affect tomorrow's meeting?

233
00:16:01,391 --> 00:16:02,521
I see.

234
00:16:03,231 --> 00:16:06,651
He won't be able to issue any orders
that would put me at a disadvantage.

235
00:16:07,441 --> 00:16:08,611
That's right.

236
00:16:09,401 --> 00:16:11,491
If he took Thorkell away from you,

237
00:16:11,571 --> 00:16:15,031
or sent you to a warzone, it would only feed the rumors.

238
00:16:16,321 --> 00:16:18,411
The king depends on public favor.

239
00:16:18,911 --> 00:16:22,711
If he gets a bad reputation among the military,
he won't be able to ignore it.

240
00:16:23,871 --> 00:16:27,131
Especially if they found out he murdered his own child.

241
00:16:29,671 --> 00:16:32,091
You're so cunning.

242
00:16:32,171 --> 00:16:34,591
Where did you learn how to do it?

243
00:16:34,681 --> 00:16:38,101
Brute force isn't the only way to fight.

244
00:16:38,181 --> 00:16:39,511
Did you learn something new?

245
00:16:40,851 --> 00:16:42,811
The king might not strike

246
00:16:42,891 --> 00:16:44,941
for the time being.

247
00:16:45,851 --> 00:16:47,401
It's a good way to buy time.

248
00:16:48,981 --> 00:16:49,981
But

249
00:16:50,071 --> 00:16:53,241
I won't let you use a double for me ever again.

250
00:16:54,111 --> 00:16:56,701
Yes. I apologize.

251
00:16:58,951 --> 00:17:02,951
I'm so impressed, Askeladd!

252
00:17:03,041 --> 00:17:05,791
I feel like I have a force of ten thousand on my side!

253
00:17:06,501 --> 00:17:08,131
Thanks.

254
00:17:08,291 --> 00:17:11,381
Well, it looks like our discussion is wrapping up.

255
00:17:11,461 --> 00:17:13,471
I'm going to run some errands now.

256
00:17:14,261 --> 00:17:17,431
Wow! Having him here is so reassuring!

257
00:17:19,931 --> 00:17:20,761
Your Highness.

258
00:17:21,771 --> 00:17:24,351
You must not trust Gunnar.

259
00:17:25,021 --> 00:17:27,101
He's probably communicating with King Sweyn.

260
00:17:28,271 --> 00:17:31,111
Why do you think so? Tell me your reason.

261
00:17:31,271 --> 00:17:34,571
It's my gut feeling. But I'm sure about it.

262
00:17:34,651 --> 00:17:38,661
Then wasn't that bad just now?
He'll find out about what we were talking about.

263
00:17:38,741 --> 00:17:40,071
I don't care.

264
00:17:40,161 --> 00:17:42,491
I've only talked about things that are superfluous.

265
00:17:43,291 --> 00:17:47,171
If Gunnar is on their side, then he's going to
tell them tonight about what he just heard.

266
00:17:47,251 --> 00:17:50,501
I asked Thorfinn to follow him to make sure.

267
00:17:51,541 --> 00:17:53,881
What are you going to do if Gunnar is a spy?

268
00:17:54,551 --> 00:17:55,671
Are you going to kill him?

269
00:17:58,051 --> 00:17:59,471
Let him work.

270
00:18:00,681 --> 00:18:04,721
We'll use him to tell the king

271
00:18:04,931 --> 00:18:06,981
that we don't want a short-term battle.

272
00:18:07,691 --> 00:18:10,691
If he hears it from his spy, he'll believe it, and relax.

273
00:18:11,441 --> 00:18:15,531
In order to avoid conflict for now, it's necessary to have
an understanding from both sides.

274
00:18:16,651 --> 00:18:19,451
My plan is complete now.

275
00:18:24,201 --> 00:18:26,331
You're unbelievable.

276
00:18:27,541 --> 00:18:31,711
I'm looking forward to seeing
the king's reaction tomorrow.

277
00:18:40,221 --> 00:18:41,511
That's the king's house.

278
00:18:41,851 --> 00:18:42,931
Now, we know for sure.

279
00:18:48,021 --> 00:18:50,901
Everyone's obsessed with deceiving each other.

280
00:18:50,981 --> 00:18:53,111
Is that what a warrior is supposed to do?

281
00:18:54,191 --> 00:18:55,571
There's only one thing

282
00:18:56,441 --> 00:18:57,281
I'm supposed to do.

283
00:19:06,451 --> 00:19:09,831
Do we really have to do this before the Imperial Council,

284
00:19:09,911 --> 00:19:11,371
Thorfinn?

285
00:19:17,171 --> 00:19:20,341
Wouldn't it be better to wait
until your right arm heals?

286
00:19:22,341 --> 00:19:25,761
Well, I'm fine with it either way.

287
00:19:25,851 --> 00:19:27,851
I shall be the witness.

288
00:19:28,931 --> 00:19:31,481
The duel is over when I tell you to stop.

289
00:19:32,061 --> 00:19:33,151
You both agree with that?

290
00:19:34,271 --> 00:19:35,691
Fine with me.

291
00:19:36,071 --> 00:19:38,691
But please wait a moment, Your Highness.

292
00:19:39,861 --> 00:19:42,321
I have a previous engagement.

293
00:19:42,411 --> 00:19:43,621
I will return later.

294
00:19:53,081 --> 00:19:55,541
Sorry, Thorfinn.

295
00:19:56,501 --> 00:19:57,801
We'll be done soon.

296
00:20:02,471 --> 00:20:05,301
Understood. Begin.

297
00:20:26,741 --> 00:20:27,781
Askeladd.

298
00:20:29,161 --> 00:20:31,501
You're strong and smart.

299
00:20:32,911 --> 00:20:34,831
I look up to you.

300
00:20:37,171 --> 00:20:38,211
Even though

301
00:20:38,881 --> 00:20:41,881
you hate me from the bottom of your heart.

302
00:20:45,221 --> 00:20:46,931
Hey, Askeladd.

303
00:20:48,101 --> 00:20:49,561
I'm not the only one.

304
00:20:50,561 --> 00:20:51,681
You hated

305
00:20:51,771 --> 00:20:53,771
our friends who died...

306
00:20:54,601 --> 00:20:56,691
and even yourself.

307
00:21:01,071 --> 00:21:02,941
Aren't you lonely?

308
00:21:04,701 --> 00:21:06,411
Rejecting everything

309
00:21:06,491 --> 00:21:08,491
like that?

310
00:21:11,041 --> 00:21:12,161
I...

311
00:21:13,081 --> 00:21:14,211
wanted...

312
00:21:17,211 --> 00:21:18,291
Wanted...

313
00:21:20,211 --> 00:21:22,511
to be friends with you.

314
00:21:48,491 --> 00:21:51,201
Sorry! I missed the vital spot! I'll put you at ease.

315
00:21:51,281 --> 00:21:53,581
Askeladd...

316
00:21:55,411 --> 00:21:57,791
I wanted to be friends with you...

317
00:22:04,301 --> 00:22:05,721
Yeah. Bjorn...

318
00:22:07,261 --> 00:22:08,221
You're

319
00:22:09,761 --> 00:22:11,431
my only

320
00:22:12,681 --> 00:22:13,721
friend.

321
00:22:28,451 --> 00:22:30,531
Send me off.

322
00:22:56,931 --> 00:23:00,481
Well, then. Sorry to keep you waiting, kid.

323
00:23:01,351 --> 00:23:02,231
Come.

324
00:23:07,691 --> 00:23:08,991
I'll play with you.
